The failures support your revised model, but the generic-seed shortcut is not yet justified: `ForLoop` and `WhileLoop` are sibling subclasses of `Loop`, so a ForLoop-target TMSC must reject a WhileLoop reference; however, **To More Generic Class still requires a Loop-typed target-class input**, so converting the ForLoop seed and then feeding that output back as TMSC?�s target does not bootstrap the missing Loop type?�it is circular unless you already possess a Loop class specifier/typed terminal ([VI Server hierarchy](https://labviewwiki.org/wiki/VI_Server_Class_Hierarchy), [NI class-specifier documentation](https://www.ni.com/docs/en-AS/bundle/labview-api-ref/page/constants/class-specifier.html)). The cheaper donor may therefore be a control created from the `reference` input of a property node explicitly configured as class `Loop`, not another concrete-loop example. Once genuinely Loop-typed, one op should accept both concrete loop classes and safely read inherited `Shift Registers[]` ID `6361402`; using that inherited property on a WhileLoop-typed TMSC output is valid because `WhileLoop` derives from `Loop` ([Loop class](https://www.labviewwiki.org/wiki/Loop_class), [WhileLoop class](https://labviewwiki.org/wiki/WhileLoop_class)). Do not add a separate condition-terminal traversal: WhileLoop already exposes `Loop End Ref` ID `6362C00`, which directly returns that terminal ([WhileLoop class](https://labviewwiki.org/wiki/WhileLoop_class)). For register traversal, the documented classes are `LeftShiftRegister` class ID `16442` and `RightShiftRegister` class ID `16399`; both inherit `Tunnel`, whose usable terminal properties are `Inside Terminals[]` `6356000` and `Outside Terminal` `6356001` ([hierarchy](https://labviewwiki.org/wiki/VI_Server_Class_Hierarchy), [Tunnel class](https://labviewwiki.org/wiki/Tunnel_class)). Pairing is explicitly available only from the left side via `Right Shift Register` ID `6374C00`; stacked left elements are added with method `6374800`, not exposed as a documented ?�paired register??array ([LeftShiftRegister class](https://www.labviewwiki.org/wiki/LeftShiftRegister_class)). Thus the risky remaining prediction is that `Shift Registers[]` returns the side/class you expect: inspect the returned refnum datatype or runtime class before designing the reader, then traverse `Inside Terminals[]`/`Outside Terminal` and `RightReg`, rather than guessing generic `Terminals[]` ordering.
